{"nodes":[{"id":"362e9f66bf03a952","type":"text","text":"[summary]\n\nFocus on ONLY Generative AI in program development for nonprofits.\n### Module 1: Program Development (Logic Models)\n**Learning Outcomes:**\n1. Understand the basics of nonprofit program development.\n2. Learn how to use generative AI to ideate and design new programs.\n3. Master the creation of logic models using generative AI to define program outcomes, activities, and resources.\n\n**Necessary Content:**\n- Introduction to program development in nonprofit management.\n- Overview of generative AI tools and their application in ideation and design.\n- Steps for creating a logic model: defining problem statements, objectives, inputs, activities, outputs, outcomes, and impact.\n- Case studies and examples of successful program development using generative AI.\n\n**Generative AI Use Cases:**\n- Ideation: Using AI to brainstorm and refine program ideas based on community needs and organizational goals.\n- Design: Developing program structure and activities through AI-generated templates and examples.\n- Logic Model Creation: Utilizing AI to articulate and visualize the logical flow from program resources (inputs) to the desired impact (outcomes).","x":-1560,"y":-194,"width":540,"height":914},{"id":"b721d13b70d028de","type":"text","text":"[topic]\nGenerative AI, ChatGPT nonprofit management, program development, logic models","x":-960,"y":-194,"width":340,"height":794},{"id":"61eba20dfe5938a4","type":"text","text":"[KB]\n\n{{[[Nonprofit Management (Course)]]}}","x":-41,"y":-194,"width":721,"height":754},{"id":"cb0c5985b7580195","type":"text","text":"[course]\n{{[[AI for Nonprofit Management (Outline)]]}}","x":-340,"y":109,"width":250,"height":264},{"id":"fd15b5781ca74dcf","type":"text","text":"[mod]\nModule 1\n","x":-620,"y":109,"width":250,"height":127},{"id":"b899d8fd05e60755","type":"text","text":"[Tone]\nProfessional, educational, engaging, practical.\n\nShow don't tell.","x":-620,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},{"id":"e4ce0f2c27c7ebf7","type":"text","text":"[skills]\n\n1. **AI Literacy**: Understanding the basics of artificial intelligence, including how generative AI operates and can be applied in various nonprofit management contexts such as program development, fundraising, stewardship, and grant writing/reporting.\n    \n2. **Data Analysis and Interpretation**: Skills in analyzing and interpreting data to inform decision-making, especially in the context of donor research, program impact assessment, and identifying grant opportunities.\n    \n3. **Strategic Thinking and Planning**: Ability to use AI tools for strategic planning, including developing logic models for program development, creating targeted fundraising strategies, and planning personalized donor stewardship approaches.\n    \n4. **Creative Problem-Solving**: Leveraging AI for ideation and design, requiring creativity to solve problems and innovate within program development, fundraising campaigns, and donor engagement strategies.\n    \n5. **Technical Proficiency with AI Tools**: Competence in navigating and utilizing specific AI tools and platforms that assist in tasks such as donor segmentation, content creation for fundraising, and automated reporting.\n    \n6. **Communication and Persuasion**: Skills in crafting persuasive and engaging content with the help of AI, including writing grant proposals, fundraising appeals, and personalized donor communications.\n    \n7. **Project Management**: Managing projects effectively, from the ideation phase with AI through to execution, including organizing fundraising campaigns, overseeing program development, and handling grant reporting processes.\n    \n8. **Ethical Consideration and Bias Awareness**: Understanding the ethical implications of using AI in nonprofit management, including issues related to data privacy, donor consent, and being aware of and mitigating biases in AI-generated content and decision-making processes.\n","x":895,"y":-823,"width":810,"height":1783},{"id":"6b08fd22e19786b1","type":"text","text":"{{[[Project Creator]]}} create a project for {{outline}}","x":-3920,"y":4363,"width":250,"height":197,"color":"4"},{"id":"e206a944b2d106de","type":"text","text":"### Module 1: Program Development with Generative AI in Nonprofit Management\n\n#### 1.1 Rationale: Understanding Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n- The importance of effective program development in achieving nonprofit goals.\n- The transformative potential of generative AI for enhancing program development processes.\n- How mastering generative AI tools can lead to innovative solutions and increased impact in the nonprofit sector.\n\n#### 1.2 Expectations: Skills Acquisition and Application\n- Learners will be able to articulate the fundamentals of nonprofit program development.\n- Learners will gain proficiency in using generative AI for program ideation and design.\n- Learners will be competent in constructing comprehensive logic models with the assistance of generative AI.\n\n#### 1.3 Pre-Assessment: Gauging Current Understanding\n- Scenario-based questions to assess knowledge of nonprofit program development.\n- Questions on the basics of generative AI and its applications in nonprofits.\n- Logic model comprehension check to identify areas for focus in the module.\n\n#### 1.4 Concepts and Theories: Foundations of Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n- Nonprofit Program Development: The lifecycle of a nonprofit program, from conception to evaluation.\n- Generative AI Overview: An introduction to generative AI, how it works, and its potential uses.\n- Logic Models Explained: The components of a logic model and their interrelationships.\n\n#### 1.5 Walkthrough: Applying Generative AI to Program Development\n- Step-by-step guide on using generative AI for program ideation, leveraging AI tools to brainstorm and refine ideas.\n- Detailed instructions on designing a program structure with AI-generated templates.\n- Creating logic models with generative AI assistance, visualizing the flow from inputs to outcomes.\n\n#### 1.6 Best Practices: Utilizing Generative AI in Nonprofit Program Development\n- Best Practices in AI-Assisted Ideation: How to use generative AI to generate and refine program ideas effectively.\n- Designing with AI: Tips for developing program structures using generative AI outputs.\n- Logic Model Construction: How to ensure clarity and coherence when building logic models with AI tools.\n\n#### 1.7 Case Study: Generative AI in Action\n- A comprehensive case study illustrating the use of generative AI in developing a nonprofit program, from ideation to logic model creation.\n- Analysis of the case study, highlighting the application of skills acquired in the module.\n- Reflection on the benefits and challenges of integrating generative AI into the program development process.\n\n#### 1.8 Application: Practicing Skills with Generative AI Tools\n- Practice Activity: Role-playing exercise using a chatbot to simulate the process of program development with generative AI.\n- Hands-on tasks for creating a draft logic model using generative AI outputs.\n- Analysis and refinement of the draft model to meet set objectives and outcomes.","x":120,"y":1880,"width":1640,"height":1600,"color":"6"},{"id":"6d4cb37e40c281eb","type":"text","text":"[audience]\nAdult learners looking to upskill or for a career change\n\nLittle or no experience with AI or Generative AI tools, so they need a lot of guidance and examples.\n\nThe audience will NOT be training models, only using available ones like chatgpt.","x":-340,"y":-194,"width":250,"height":220},{"id":"18795c84f0d61402","type":"text","text":"#### 1.1 Rationale: Understanding Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n\nIn the vast and dynamic sector of nonprofit management, the ability to develop impactful programs is paramount. Programs are the vehicles through which nonprofits deliver their mission to the community, address pressing issues, and create lasting change. However, crafting these programs requires strategic planning, an understanding of community needs, and the capacity to measure success. \n\nThe integration of generative AI into this process marks a significant stride forward. Generative AI refers to artificial intelligence that can generate new content based on the data it has been trained on. For nonprofits, this means the ability to automate and enhance various aspects of program development, from brainstorming ideas to creating detailed operational plans. By incorporating generative AI, nonprofits can achieve higher levels of creativity, efficiency, and effectiveness.\n\nFor those in the nonprofit sector, learning to harness the capabilities of generative AI is not just an exercise in technical proficiency; it is about embracing a tool that can amplify impact. Imagine a scenario where you can instantly generate a range of potential solutions to a community problem, draft grant proposals, or even create personalized communication materials for your audience—all with the support of AI.\n\nThe benefits of mastering generative AI tools are multifaceted:\n- **Efficiency**: Automating tasks that traditionally take up considerable time allows staff to focus on strategic decisions and human-centered work.\n- **Innovation**: Generative AI can provide unexpected perspectives and ideas, pushing the boundaries of traditional program design.\n- **Precision**: AI tools can assist in creating more accurate and data-driven logic models, leading to better alignment of activities and desired outcomes.\n\nFor those aiming to make a significant impact in their nonprofit roles, understanding and utilizing generative AI is not just advantageous—it is becoming essential. This module will equip you with the knowledge and skills to be at the forefront of this technological advancement, ensuring that your programs resonate with both the heart and the intelligence of what AI can offer.","x":-2600,"y":1880,"width":888,"height":1147,"color":"6"},{"id":"edd7a949f8bba0d1","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}}, act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{1}} to write ONLY EXPECTATIONS {{[mod]}}.2 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":-1154,"y":4381,"width":319,"height":441,"color":"4"},{"id":"30b1b35aa9ab0f19","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and write ONLY RATIONALE {{[mod]}}.1 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":-2156,"y":4419,"width":319,"height":324,"color":"4"},{"id":"473d4bbb63eb4647","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{2}} to write ONLY PRE-ASSESSMENT {{[mod]}}.3 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. \n\nEnsure all of the questions have the correct answer bolded, and a detailed explanation as to why it is correct.","x":-320,"y":4421,"width":319,"height":401,"color":"4"},{"id":"dce5df780ab52cad","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{3}} to write ONLY CONCEPTS AND THEORIES {{[mod]}}.4 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":595,"y":4401,"width":319,"height":441,"color":"4"},{"id":"b71fc4b1670d8202","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{4}} to write ONLY WALKTHROUGH {{[mod]}}.5 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":1412,"y":4380,"width":319,"height":484,"color":"4"},{"id":"ddec3972db6f7243","type":"text","text":"{{[[Knowledge Checker]]}} create no more than 3 knowledge checks for {{5}}, each with the correct answer identified, and an explanation.","x":1040,"y":4991,"width":250,"height":486,"color":"3"},{"id":"db68b69110362415","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{5}} to write ONLY BEST PRACTICES {{[mod]}}.6 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":2240,"y":4383,"width":319,"height":481,"color":"3"},{"id":"fb56a7aa60ff43ff","type":"text","text":"{{[[Knowledge Checker]]}} create no more than 3 knowledge checks for {{6}}, each with the correct answer identified, and an explanation.","x":1731,"y":4991,"width":250,"height":486,"color":"0"},{"id":"971d3f36f09c8940","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{1}} to {{6}} write ONLY CASE STUDY {{[mod]}}.7 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. \n\n","x":3040,"y":4421,"width":319,"height":400,"color":"0"},{"id":"909f15933e2fc5a6","type":"text","text":"{{[[SubModule Author]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}, and continue from {{8}} to write ONLY ACTIVITY {{mod}}.8 of {{outline}} in {{[Tone]}} tone for {{[audience]}} audience using knowledge base {{[KB]}}. ","x":3920,"y":4401,"width":319,"height":440,"color":"0"},{"id":"7fb17253362602bd","type":"text","text":"{{[[Knowledge Checker]]}} create no more than 3 knowledge checks for {{7}}, each with the correct answer identified, and an explanation.","x":3234,"y":4895,"width":250,"height":486,"color":"0"},{"id":"2e25d084af8fe1e9","type":"text","text":"{{[[Module Concluder]]}} write the conclusion for {{mod}}, based on {{1}}, {{2}}, {{3}}, {{4}}, {{5}}, {{6}}, {{7}}, {{8}}","x":4640,"y":4424,"width":250,"height":399,"color":"0"},{"id":"a20c223abafa63e0","type":"text","text":"{{[[Module Introducer]]}} introduce {{outline}}","x":-3200,"y":4461,"width":355,"height":240,"color":"4"},{"id":"942b2971771b8692","type":"text","text":"Create flash cards based on {{4}}, for each concept and theory provided to the learner.","x":345,"y":5080,"width":250,"height":486,"color":"4"},{"id":"7473cc1c6c72e117","type":"text","text":"{{[[Outline Expander]]}} act as an expert in {{[topic]}}. Expand ONLY {{[mod]}} combine the {{[summary]}} into the 8 subtopics (rationale, expectations, pre-assessment, concepts and theories, walkthrough, best practices, case study, application) using {{[KB]}} as a knowledge base for {{[audience]}} learn {{[skills]}} ","x":740,"y":1240,"width":399,"height":560,"color":"4"},{"id":"a8171d1d12c82f74","type":"text","text":"## 1.4 Concepts and Theories: Foundations of Nonprofit Program Development and Generative AI\n\nWelcome to the foundational building blocks of nonprofit program development and the intriguing world of generative AI. As we delve into these concepts, remember that the goal is to enhance your capability to design and implement effective nonprofit programs. We will also demystify generative AI, ensuring you can leverage this technology to amplify your organization's impact. Let's begin.\n\n### Nonprofit Program Development: The Lifecycle\nIn the nonprofit sector, programs are the vehicles through which mission-driven initiatives are delivered. The lifecycle of a nonprofit program typically involves these stages:\n\n1. **Needs Assessment:** Identifying the needs that the program aims to address, usually through community surveys, research, and data analysis.\n2. **Program Planning:** Outlining the program's objectives, strategies, resources needed, and stakeholders involved.\n3. **Implementation:** The activation phase where plans are executed, and activities are carried out.\n4. **Monitoring:** Ongoing oversight to ensure the program is on track, making adjustments as necessary.\n5. **Evaluation:** Assessing the program's effectiveness in achieving its goals and objectives, and determining the impact on the target population.\n6. **Reporting and Reflection:** Sharing results with stakeholders and using insights gained to inform future programming.\n\n**Example**: Consider a program aimed at reducing food insecurity in a local community. The lifecycle begins with assessing the extent of food scarcity issues among residents. Planning would involve setting up food distribution centers, while implementation would see these centers operational. Monitoring ensures the centers run efficiently, and evaluation would determine if food insecurity rates are declining. Finally, reporting involves sharing these outcomes with donors, volunteers, and the community.\n\n### Generative AI Overview: Enhancement through Technology\nGenerative AI refers to artificial intelligence that can generate content, ideas, or data that did not exist before. It uses machine learning algorithms to analyze patterns and make predictions. For nonprofits, generative AI can:\n\n1. **Idea Generation:** Produce creative solutions for program development by synthesizing vast amounts of information.\n2. **Content Creation:** Draft grant proposals, reports, and marketing material.\n3. **Data Analysis:** Interpret large datasets to inform decision-making and needs assessment.\n4. **Automation:** Streamline repetitive tasks, allowing staff to focus on strategic functions.\n\n**Example**: A generative AI tool could be fed information about trends in voluntary work and generate a list of innovative volunteer engagement strategies that your nonprofit might not have considered.\n\n### Logic Models Explained: Visualizing Success\nA logic model is a visual representation that links the resources you have (inputs) to the activities you plan (outputs) and the changes or benefits you hope to achieve (outcomes). It usually includes:\n\n- **Inputs:** What we invest, such as time, money, staff, volunteers, and equipment.\n- **Activities:** What the program does with the inputs to fulfill its mission, like workshops, services, and events.\n- **Outputs:** The direct results of program activities, often quantified as the number of services delivered or participants served.\n- **Outcomes:** The specific changes or benefits that result from the program, in the short, medium, or long term.\n\n**Example**: For a literacy program for seniors, inputs may include trained volunteers, educational materials, and a dedicated space for classes. Activities are the actual classes and workshops. Outputs could be the number of seniors who attend these classes, while outcomes might include improved digital literacy among participants.\n\nBy the end of this section, you should possess a foundational understanding of the stages and considerations involved in nonprofit program development, the transformative potential of generative AI, and the strategic framework provided by logic models. These concepts are not just academic; they are practical tools that will empower you to elevate your nonprofit's work to new heights of efficiency and effectiveness. As we progress, remember these theories are your scaffolding, supporting the real-world application of skills that will soon become part of your professional repertoire.","x":-1361,"y":2220,"width":1041,"height":1420,"color":"6"},{"id":"5b70ce041eb2e740","type":"text","text":"## 1.5 Walkthrough: Applying Generative AI to Program Development\n\nIn this section, we'll guide you through the process of harnessing generative AI to streamline and enhance your nonprofit program development. Imagine you are at the helm of a new initiative, and generative AI is your first officer, ready to assist you in charting a course through the oftentimes choppy waters of program planning and execution.\n\n### Utilizing Generative AI for Program Ideation\n\nFirst, let's focus on using generative AI to generate innovative program ideas:\n\n1. **Define the Challenge:** Clearly state the problem your nonprofit seeks to address. For instance, \"We need to increase community engagement in our urban sustainability program.\"\n\n2. **Input Data into AI:** Using a generative AI tool, input the challenge along with any relevant background information, such as target demographics, previous initiatives, and constraints.\n\n3. **Generate Ideas:** Prompt the AI to generate a list of program ideas. For example, you could ask, \"What are some innovative ways to engage urban communities in sustainability programs?\"\n\n4. **Refine Suggestions:** Review the AI-generated ideas, select the most promising ones, and refine them further. You might ask the AI to expand on a particular idea, or to combine elements from several ideas into a new concept.\n\n**Example**: The AI suggests creating a mobile app that gamifies sustainable practices. You could then ask the AI to flesh out how the gamification mechanics would work and what incentives might motivate users.\n\n### Designing a Program Structure with AI-Generated Templates\n\nOnce you have a solid idea, you'll need to structure your program:\n\n1. **Request Templates:** Ask the generative AI for specific templates related to program planning, such as a project charter or a work breakdown structure.\n\n2. **Customization:** Take the AI-generated template and customize it with the specifics of your program. Insert your objectives, activities, and target outcomes.\n\n3. **Iterative Feedback:** Use the AI to review and provide feedback on your draft. It can suggest improvements or highlight areas that may require more detail.\n\n**Example**: If the AI provides a template for a project charter, you would fill in the details about your mobile app's development, including timelines, resource allocation, and key performance indicators.\n\n### Creating Logic Models with Generative AI Assistance\n\nFinally, visualize the flow from inputs to outcomes using a logic model:\n\n1. **Request a Logic Model Template:** Prompt the AI to generate a blank logic model template.\n\n2. **Fill in the Components:** Using the information about your program, populate each section of the logic model: inputs, activities, outputs, and outcomes.\n\n3. **Evaluation Planning:** Ask the AI to suggest methods for evaluating each outcome, ensuring that your program has measurable success indicators.\n\n**Example**: For the mobile app, inputs would include software development resources, while activities might involve coding, testing, and user feedback sessions. Outputs could be the number of app downloads, and outcomes might be measured by the increase in reported sustainable practices among users.\n\nAs you progress through these steps, remember that generative AI is a tool to augment your expertise and creativity. It can provide a multitude of options and save you time, but the final decisions and judgments rest with you and your team. Use the AI's suggestions as a starting point, and then apply your knowledge of your community and your organization's strengths to tailor the program to your needs.\n\nThrough this walkthrough, you've seen how generative AI can act as a co-pilot in program development, helping you generate ideas, structure your plans, and create a roadmap for success. By incorporating these steps into your workflow, you'll be better equipped to design programs that are both innovative and impactful.","x":2034,"y":2254,"width":1050,"height":886,"color":"6"},{"id":"fa8e408b339af0b3","type":"text","text":"\"\"{{intro}}\n\n{{1}}\n\n{{2}}\n\n{{3}}\n\n{{4}}\n\n{{quiz4}}\n\n{{5}}\n\n{{quiz5}}\n\n{{6}}\n\n{{quiz6}}\n\n{{7}}\n\n{{8}}\n\n{{quiz8}}\n\n{{end}}\n\n{{project}}\"\"","x":505,"y":6320,"width":250,"height":310,"color":"6"},{"id":"385538c9f6e1c7bf","type":"text","text":"","x":230,"y":6960,"width":800,"height":1240,"color":"6"}],"edges":[{"id":"ee78fed8d9346629","fromNode":"7473cc1c6c72e117","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"e206a944b2d106de","toSide":"top"},{"id":"fd2b8178cae19237","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"6b08fd22e19786b1","toSide":"right"},{"id":"29d5ae5611e80531","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"30b1b35aa9ab0f19","toSide":"top","label":"outline"},{"id":"f4267fdbfb13ac5e","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"edd7a949f8bba0d1","toSide":"top"},{"id":"ab461411ea050dbe","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"a20c223abafa63e0","toSide":"top"},{"id":"da7902b31c500131","fromNode":"a20c223abafa63e0","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"left","label":"intro"},{"id":"c2f78e66543a3967","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"473d4bbb63eb4647","toSide":"top"},{"id":"c761c1b08fda036f","fromNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"942b2971771b8692","toSide":"top","label":"4"},{"id":"5aebc33cd8880a13","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","toSide":"top"},{"id":"06b4ee85c56e44bd","fromNode":"942b2971771b8692","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"quiz4"},{"id":"93b2b2532fc262b1","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","toSide":"top"},{"id":"95d3f0ced712b5f3","fromNode":"ddec3972db6f7243","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"quiz5"},{"id":"a03fe5b43183d775","fromNode":"db68b69110362415","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fb56a7aa60ff43ff","toSide":"top"},{"id":"5c6aab12cba030ed","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"db68b69110362415","toSide":"top"},{"id":"9af6ff47db4406b9","fromNode":"fb56a7aa60ff43ff","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"quiz6"},{"id":"3fe1e3be6ef07685","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"971d3f36f09c8940","toSide":"top"},{"id":"36a50354b0d7d565","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"909f15933e2fc5a6","toSide":"top"},{"id":"9c1497ff23dfb915","fromNode":"6b08fd22e19786b1","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"left","label":"project"},{"id":"41ac5b8528dd006f","fromNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"385538c9f6e1c7bf","toSide":"top"},{"id":"3276645c088bc297","fromNode":"7fb17253362602bd","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"quiz8"},{"id":"df28b235bbe648f1","fromNode":"30b1b35aa9ab0f19","fromSide":"right","toNode":"edd7a949f8bba0d1","toSide":"left","label":"1"},{"id":"30ca4487b260ed15","fromNode":"edd7a949f8bba0d1","fromSide":"right","toNode":"473d4bbb63eb4647","toSide":"left","label":"2"},{"id":"34fbd24fc5773120","fromNode":"473d4bbb63eb4647","fromSide":"right","toNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","toSide":"left","label":"3"},{"id":"c24fc812ccecaa52","fromNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","fromSide":"right","toNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","toSide":"left","label":"4"},{"id":"c4a580affa3bf2bf","fromNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","fromSide":"right","toNode":"db68b69110362415","toSide":"left","label":"5"},{"id":"d9d83f89bd885445","fromNode":"db68b69110362415","fromSide":"right","toNode":"971d3f36f09c8940","toSide":"left","label":"6"},{"id":"558509131f477ff5","fromNode":"971d3f36f09c8940","fromSide":"right","toNode":"909f15933e2fc5a6","toSide":"left","label":"7"},{"id":"9816d75e3a62dd37","fromNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"ddec3972db6f7243","toSide":"top"},{"id":"31c5e1ce7c940218","fromNode":"909f15933e2fc5a6","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"7fb17253362602bd","toSide":"top"},{"id":"ac36661afdf83484","fromNode":"909f15933e2fc5a6","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"8"},{"id":"6eab3caf426b7675","fromNode":"edd7a949f8bba0d1","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"2"},{"id":"e89e4fdde91d6746","fromNode":"473d4bbb63eb4647","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"3"},{"id":"eb74503518ff484c","fromNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"4"},{"id":"3c5185f43c63bbf2","fromNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"top","label":"5"},{"id":"9b918edb9d4972b3","fromNode":"db68b69110362415","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"6"},{"id":"36e8a36b164c9563","fromNode":"971d3f36f09c8940","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"7"},{"id":"5cdea98b1d74323a","fromNode":"e206a944b2d106de","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"2e25d084af8fe1e9","toSide":"top"},{"id":"f6ed7d0e641b77d7","fromNode":"2e25d084af8fe1e9","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"right","label":"end"},{"id":"920a67dd55d0bddf","fromNode":"30b1b35aa9ab0f19","fromSide":"top","toNode":"18795c84f0d61402","toSide":"bottom"},{"id":"8b648797583c45ea","fromNode":"909f15933e2fc5a6","fromSide":"right","toNode":"2e25d084af8fe1e9","toSide":"left"},{"id":"8b996cae0d2219b6","fromNode":"30b1b35aa9ab0f19","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"fa8e408b339af0b3","toSide":"left","label":"1"},{"id":"4c5290735d082958","fromNode":"dce5df780ab52cad","fromSide":"top","toNode":"a8171d1d12c82f74","toSide":"bottom"},{"id":"61f9f20d721f4dcb","fromNode":"b71fc4b1670d8202","fromSide":"top","toNode":"5b70ce041eb2e740","toSide":"bottom"}]}